camera|picture-device|NOUN|Device for photographs|A device that captures visual images as photographs.|máy ảnh; thiết bị chụp ảnh|Bao adjusted the camera before photographing the old bridge.|Bảo chỉnh máy ảnh trước khi chụp cây cầu cũ.|Camera is countable; take a photograph with a camera identifies the equipment used.|camera
ear|hearing-part|NOUN|Part of the body for hearing|The part of a person's or animal's body used for hearing, including its visible outer part.|tai; bộ phận cơ thể dùng để nghe|The puppy lifted one ear when the door opened.|Con chó con vểnh một tai lên khi cửa mở.|Ear is countable; ears is the plural, and in someone's ear can describe where a whisper is directed.|ear
tattoo|skin-design|NOUN|Lasting skin design|A lasting picture or pattern made by putting coloured pigment into the skin with needles.|hình xăm|The musician has a small leaf tattoo on her wrist.|Nữ nhạc công có một hình xăm chiếc lá nhỏ trên cổ tay.|Tattoo is countable; get a tattoo describes having one made and have a tattoo describes possessing it.|tattoo
hospital|medical-institution|NOUN|Place for medical care|An institution where people who are ill or injured receive medical care and treatment.|bệnh viện|The hospital opened a new ward for children.|Bệnh viện mở một khoa mới dành cho trẻ em.|Hospital is countable; British English often uses in hospital for a patient, while American English commonly uses in the hospital.|hospital
interesting|holds-attention|ADJECTIVE|Holding attention|Causing curiosity or making someone want to learn more.|thú vị; gây chú ý hoặc tò mò|The interesting display showed how paper is recycled.|Khu trưng bày thú vị cho thấy giấy được tái chế như thế nào.|Interesting describes what holds attention; interested describes the person who feels that attention.|interesting
freshwater|non-salty-water|NOUN|Water with little salt|Water containing very little dissolved salt, such as water in many rivers and lakes.|nước ngọt; nước có rất ít muối hòa tan|The stream supplies freshwater to the village.|Con suối cung cấp nước ngọt cho ngôi làng.|Freshwater names water in this proposal; before a noun, as in freshwater lake, it describes a connection with that water.|freshwater
festival|celebratory-event|NOUN|Organized celebration|An organized event or series of events celebrating music, a tradition or another subject.|lễ hội; chuỗi hoạt động tổ chức để kỷ niệm hoặc tôn vinh một chủ đề|The village festival includes dancing and a lantern parade.|Lễ hội của làng có múa và diễu hành đèn lồng.|Festival is countable; at a festival refers to attending its activities and a music festival identifies its subject.|festival
something|unspecified-thing|PRONOUN|Unspecified thing or matter|A thing or matter that is not named or described precisely.|thứ gì đó; điều gì đó chưa được nêu rõ|Something shiny was lying beside the gate.|Một thứ gì đó sáng bóng nằm bên cạnh cổng.|Something takes a singular verb; an adjective normally follows it, as in something shiny.|something
arrogant|superior-attitude|ADJECTIVE|Behaving as if superior|Believing and behaving as though you are more important or better than other people.|kiêu ngạo; tự cho mình hơn người khác|His arrogant manner made the new volunteers uncomfortable.|Thái độ kiêu ngạo của anh ấy khiến những tình nguyện viên mới cảm thấy không thoải mái.|Arrogant describes a person or their behaviour and carries criticism; it is different from simply being confident.|arrogant
opinion|personal-view|NOUN|Personal judgment or belief|A judgment or belief that someone holds about a person, thing or situation.|ý kiến; quan điểm hoặc nhận định cá nhân|I asked the readers for their opinion of the final chapter.|Tôi hỏi độc giả ý kiến của họ về chương cuối.|Opinion is countable; use in my opinion to introduce your view and an opinion of or about something to name its subject.|opinion
january|month-one|NOUN|First month|The first month of a calendar year.|tháng Một|The swimming classes will resume in January.|Các lớp học bơi sẽ tiếp tục trở lại vào tháng Một.|Write January with a capital J; use in January for a month and on with a specific date.|January
interested|want-to-learn|ADJECTIVE|Wanting to learn or participate|Wanting to know more about something or become involved in it.|quan tâm; có hứng thú tìm hiểu hoặc tham gia|Linh is interested in restoring old furniture.|Linh quan tâm đến việc phục chế đồ nội thất cũ.|Use interested in followed by a noun or an -ing form; interesting describes the thing that attracts attention.|interested
straw|drinking-tube|NOUN|Tube for drinking|A narrow tube through which someone draws a drink into their mouth.|ống hút dùng để uống|The café served the iced drink with a paper straw.|Quán cà phê phục vụ đồ uống lạnh kèm một ống hút giấy.|Straw is countable in this sense; drink through a straw identifies the tool used.|straw
magazine|periodical|NOUN|Regular publication|A publication issued regularly, containing articles, stories or pictures on particular subjects.|tạp chí; ấn phẩm phát hành định kỳ|The gardening magazine featured a guide to growing herbs.|Tạp chí làm vườn đăng một bài hướng dẫn trồng các loại rau thơm.|Magazine is countable; a monthly magazine is issued each month and a magazine article is one piece within it.|magazine
anyone|any-person|PRONOUN|Any person at all|Any person, without selecting a particular individual.|bất kỳ ai; một người bất kỳ|Anyone who finds the missing scarf can leave it at reception.|Bất kỳ ai tìm thấy chiếc khăn bị thất lạc có thể để nó ở quầy tiếp tân.|Anyone takes a singular verb; any one written as two words emphasizes one member of a set.|anyone
deaf|hearing-loss|ADJECTIVE|Having severe hearing loss|Unable to hear, or having very little ability to hear.|điếc; không nghe được hoặc nghe rất hạn chế|The deaf artist explained her painting through an interpreter.|Nữ họa sĩ điếc giải thích bức tranh của mình thông qua một phiên dịch viên.|Deaf can describe a person or their hearing condition; it does not imply that every deaf person communicates in the same way.|deaf
boat|watercraft|NOUN|Vessel for water travel|A vessel used to carry people or things over water.|thuyền; tàu dùng để di chuyển trên nước|The wooden boat carried baskets of vegetables across the canal.|Chiếc thuyền gỗ chở những giỏ rau qua con kênh.|Boat is countable; by boat names the means of travel and on a boat describes being aboard.|boat
meaning|sense-of-expression|NOUN|What an expression communicates|The idea or information communicated by a word, sign or statement.|nghĩa; nội dung được từ, dấu hiệu hoặc lời nói biểu đạt|The teacher explained the meaning of the unfamiliar symbol.|Giáo viên giải thích ý nghĩa của ký hiệu lạ.|Use the meaning of an expression; a word can have several meanings in different contexts.|meaning
honor|show-respect|VERB|Show respect|Show respect or appreciation for a person or thing.|tôn vinh; bày tỏ sự kính trọng|The school will honor the volunteers at a special assembly.|Nhà trường sẽ tôn vinh các tình nguyện viên trong một buổi tập hợp đặc biệt.|Honor takes a direct object in this sense; honour is the usual British spelling.|honor
fruit|edible-plant-produce|NOUN|Plant produce eaten as food|Plant produce such as apples and oranges, commonly eaten for its sweet or sharp taste.|trái cây; hoa quả dùng làm thực phẩm|We packed fresh fruit in a basket for the journey.|Chúng tôi xếp trái cây tươi vào một chiếc giỏ cho chuyến đi.|Fruit is usually uncountable when referring to food collectively; fruits can distinguish different kinds.|fruit
